  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Trolley
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: trolley
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 1
  _narratorPrompt: Oh good, you are back. Someone left a trolley running and five
    strangers standing in its way. There is one more soul on the side track, and
    a lever by your hand that decides whose morning ends here. You did enjoy deciding
    what people deserved, once. And you did know your way around a moving vehicle.
    Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: You pulled it. One traded for five, and you barely blinked. Tidy.
      Proportionate. The judge in you would have signed off without even looking
      up.
    _narratorReactStruck: 
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty: 
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 87
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
    - _axis: 2
      _value: -1
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: Hands in your pockets, five gone under, a clean conscience you
      did not quite earn. Not my lever, not my fault. You told yourself something
      like that about the last machine you were steering, too.
    _narratorReactStruck: 
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty: 
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 13
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
    - _axis: 2
      _value: 1
  _statsHeading: how others chose
  _crowdSafeFraction: 0.43
  _crowdThreshold: 0.5
  _thresholdLabel: the line
